# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production workflow exports stay local.
#
# An n8n export carries real identifiers: app ids, API project ids,
# service-account emails, warehouse database/schema paths, survey ids, and
# whatever a colleague happened to type into a sticky note. None of that
# belongs in a public repo.
#
# The rule is generic on purpose: nothing at the repo root is shared. Export a
# workflow from n8n, drop it here, and it is untracked by default. A file only
# becomes public once you have deliberately sanitised it into generic/.
#
# (This pattern is root-only, so generic/*.json is unaffected.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.json

# Anything explicitly marked as unsanitised, wherever it lives
*.private.json
*-internal.*
*-prod.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. These should never exist in the working tree at all, but belt and braces:
# the Apple key is a .p8, the Google service account is a JSON key file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
